{{!-- One labelled checkbox in a settings submenu, with its hint under it.

      Three shapes used to write this out separately: the master toggle at the top of each menu,
      and every row of the hover-descriptions list. They differ only in the field name, the id and
      where the two strings come from, so they are all this partial now.

      "name" is the form field the menu's update reads back, and "id" is only there to tie the
      label to the input. Pass label/hint already localized, or labelKey/hintKey to have it done
      here — the hover menu localizes per row in getData, the master toggles do not.

      The box sits INSIDE the label and to the LEFT of the title, which is where the character
      sheet's Preferences tab puts it (tab-preferences.hbs) — and that tab's "More…" button is
      how this window is reached, so a box that jumped to the far right one click later would
      read as a different kind of control. Inside the label also means the whole title line
      toggles it, the way every checklist on these sheets behaves.

      No "form-fields" wrapper any more: it exists to hold a control at the row's right edge,
      and there is no longer one there. Nothing reads it — FormDataExtended collects a named
      input wherever in the form it sits — so it was a div that only moved the box away from
      its own label. --}}
<div class="form-group stonetop-settings-toggle">
	<label class="stonetop-settings-toggle-label" for="stonetop-{{id}}">
		<input id="stonetop-{{id}}" type="checkbox" class="stonetop-check" name="{{name}}" {{#if checked}}checked{{/if}}>
		<span>{{#if labelKey}}{{localize labelKey}}{{else}}{{label}}{{/if}}</span>
	</label>
	<p class="notes">{{#if hintKey}}{{localize hintKey}}{{else}}{{hint}}{{/if}}</p>
</div>
